<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cornĭcŭlum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		dim.
		cornu, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little horn.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop., <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 42,
				67, § 143</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 28, 34, §
			100</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A small tunnel of horn</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 7, 5,
				15</span></i> and 20.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A horn-shaped ornament upon the helmet, as a reward
				for bravery</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 10, 44, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aur. Vict.
			723</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram. 9</span></i>; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 10,
				43, 60, § 124</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
